ffs are generally lower.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/13/bloom-energy-corporation-be-q2-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BE 2019 Q3","e":"be","d":"2019-11-07","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Randy Furr","x":"As I mentioned in the past, both ASP and TISC are impacted by a number of factors to include site location and applicable utility tariffs for that relocation whether the site includes grid outage protection and or is mission critical, the size of the site being installed.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/08/bloom-energy-corporation-be-q3-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BE 2019 Q3","e":"be","d":"2019-11-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Randy Furr","x":"…significantly higher, and we are -- as we continue with this flywheel that I talked about of our cost reduction going to get to a point, that building a large power plant using these servers this way will be cheaper than building a large scale power plant. So we will come full cycle extremely…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/08/bloom-energy-corporation-be-q3-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BE 2019 Q4","e":"be","d":"2020-03-16","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Randy Furr","x":"…ASP and TISC are impacted by a number of factors to include site location and applicable utility tariffs for that location; whether the site includes grid outage protection and/or is mission-critical; the size of the site being installed, generally, the larger the installation, the lower the…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/03/17/bloom-energy-corporation-be-q4-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BE 2019 Q4","e":"be","d":"2020-03-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Randy Furr","x":"While I'm on the topic of cost, I'd like to take this opportunity to say 2019 was another excellent year in our product cost-reduction efforts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/03/17/bloom-energy-corporation-be-q4-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BE 2019 Q4","e":"be","d":"2020-03-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Randy Furr","x":"We expect operating expenses to be between $48 million and $51 million, and this includes $3 million to $4 million of onetime expenses related to the restatement and restructuring.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/03/17/bloom-energy-corporation-be-q4-2019-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BE 2020 Q1","e":"be","d":"2020-05-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Greg Cameron","x":"I talked a little bit before about the installation cost being a little bit different, and that would drive an increase in revenue but not an increase in margin as that's a pass-through to our customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/12/bloom-energy-corporation-be-q1-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BE 2020 Q1","e":"be","d":"2020-05-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Greg Cameron","x":"We've implemented measures to preserve cash and streamline our operations by pausing some capital investments, reducing operating expenditures and deferring planned increases in production.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/12/bloom-energy-corporation-be-q1-2020-earnings-call.aspx"},{"c":"BE 2021 Q3","e":"be","d":"2021-11-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"K.R. Sridhar","x":"Both Greg and I will answer this question, Stephen and I will get started and then I will pass it on to Greg.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/05/bloom-energy-corp-be-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcr/"},{"c":"BE 2021 Q3","e":"be","d":"2021-11-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"K.R. Sridhar","x":"Here is what I think Stephen, you know from knowing this company for a long time, cost reduction is in our DNA.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/05/bloom-energy-corp-be-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcr/"},{"c":"BE 2021 Q3","e":"be","d":"2021-11-04"